<main id="main" class="shell legal"><p class="legal-date">Last reviewed 27 October 2026</p><h1>About MedPally Find</h1>
<p class="legal-lead">MedPally Find is a free directory of cardiology and cardiac critical care learning resources: tools, apps, courses, guidelines and references. It's run by Ike, a cardiology registrar in England.</p>
<h2>Why it exists</h2><p>Good cardiology teaching is scattered. A useful echo guide turns up in a social media thread, a colleague mentions a pacing course on a night shift, a brilliant ECG library gets bookmarked and forgotten. I wanted one place to keep the good ones, and somewhere to point the junior doctors and colleagues who ask me where to learn this stuff.</p>
<h2>Who runs it</h2><p>I'm Ike, a cardiology specialty registrar training in England. Before cardiology I did internal medicine training on the Mersey rotation. I'm learning echo, pacing and coronary angiography myself, so a lot of what's listed here is what I've found useful along the way. I write about training and life as an NHS doctor at <a href="https://realikechukwu.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">realikechukwu.com</a>.</p>
<h2>What gets listed</h2><ul><li>Resources for learning or practising cardiology and cardiac critical care, for doctors, nurses, physiologists, students and anyone else in the team.</li><li>Free and paid resources, as long as paid ones are worth the money. Listings show the price where I've been able to confirm it.</li><li>Things that work and that you can actually get to. Dead links and abandoned projects are hidden.</li></ul><p>Being listed isn't an endorsement, and leaving something out isn't a judgement. Plenty of good resources simply haven't been added yet.</p>
<h2>How listings are added</h2><p>Every listing starts from a link I've chosen, or a public suggestion I've approved. I draft summaries with help from AI, using the resource's own pages. They cover what it is, who made it, what it costs and which platforms it runs on. When something can't be confirmed, the listing says so. If you spot a mistake, <a href="mailto:hello@marlosolutions.com?subject=MedPally%20Find%3A%20listing%20correction">tell me</a> and I'll fix it.</p><p>Know a resource that should be here? <a href="/suggest/">Suggest it</a>. I review every suggestion before it goes live.</p>
<h2>Independence</h2><p>Nobody pays to be listed and there are no sponsored listings. If I ever have a personal link to something listed, its listing will say so. MedPally Find is published by Marlo Solutions Ltd.</p>
<h2>Get in touch</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@marlosolutions.com?subject=MedPally%20Find">hello@marlosolutions.com</a> for corrections, removals or anything else.</p>
<h2>Disclaimer</h2><p>Listings link to third-party resources. They are not clinical advice or endorsements; always check against local guidance.</p>
